# Translation Review — 人生百问 (Self-Review)

## General Notes

Overall the translation is accurate and the terminology broadly aligns with the MPI terms database (e.g., 三级修学 → Three-Stage Practice, 皈依三宝 → take refuge in the Three Jewels, 共业 → collective karma, 禅宗 → Chan). The main opportunities are in conversational flow, removing formal/literal phrasing, and tightening a few key terms.

---

## Chapter 1 — 走入佛门 / I. Entering the Dharma Door

### Q01 善用理性但不作为唯一标准

Quoted text: `I haven't taken refuge yet, because reason keeps me from fully accepting certain points of Dharma, and I feel that taking refuge hastily would be dishonest.`

- “certain points of Dharma” is slightly awkward; prefer “certain points of the Dharma” or “certain Dharma teachings.”
- “taking refuge hastily” for 贸然皈依 is understandable but stiff; “taking refuge lightly” or “taking refuge without being ready” is more natural.

Quoted text: `Animals are fine once they have eaten and drunk their fill, but after people have their basic needs met, their delusive thoughts still fly about and their afflictions weigh heavily, and when humans turn bad, they outdo animals by far.`

- “delusive thoughts still fly about” is a literal rendering of 妄念纷飞; consider “their delusions run wild.”
- “outdo animals by far” misrenders 望尘莫及 (animals cannot catch up); suggest “animals cannot compare” or “are left far behind.”
- Long sentence with three clauses; split for readability.

Quoted text: `we must use reason skillfully; otherwise it will bring trouble.`

- 善用理性 is the title theme; “use reason skillfully” is fine, but “use reason well” or “use reason wisely” sounds more conversational.

Quoted text: `we must accept a wisdom culture and have a correct understanding of life and the world`

- “wisdom culture” is an unusual collocation; consider “a wisdom tradition” or “a culture of wisdom.”

Quoted text: `Therefore we should not become fanatical rationalists who take reason as the only standard for knowing the world and hope that reason can explain and solve every problem.`

- 偏执的理性主义者：偏执 is closer to “biased / dogmatic / obsessive” than “fanatical.” Prefer “dogmatic rationalists.”
- Sentence is long and top-heavy; split after “world.”

Quoted text: `"Words are cut off, and mental activity ceases."`

- 言语道断、心行处灭 is a Chan expression. “Words are cut off” is literal; consider "Words fail, and mental activity ceases" or "Where words fall silent and mental activity ceases."

### Q02 解脱的本身就是意义

Quoted text: `worldly people bustle about for liberation too`

- “bustle about” is literary; prefer “rush about” or “busy themselves.”

Quoted text: `starting a family is for liberation from singlehood`

- “singlehood” is formal; prefer “being single” or “single life.”

Quoted text: `Seen only from the surface, people feel that youth, love, wealth, and career are all worth pursuing; if one is liberated, how can these dreams be realized?`

- “Seen only from the surface” is close to the Chinese but reads as translationese; prefer “On the surface” or “From a surface view.”
- “if one is liberated, how can these dreams be realized?” — the logic is slightly off; the Chinese asks “if one is liberated, how can these dreams still be realized?” Add “still.”

Quoted text: `the nature of samsara: the confusion and afflictions within our minds`

- 迷惑 in Buddhist contexts is often “delusion” rather than “confusion.” Prefer “delusion and affliction.”

Quoted text: `Once we are liberated from confusion and karma`

- 惑业 → terms DB gives “delusion and karma.” Prefer “delusion and karma.”

Quoted text: `The reason the Buddha attained great freedom is precisely that he was liberated from confusion and karma and opened up boundless compassion and wisdom.`

- 大自在 → terms DB: “freedom and comfort.” “Great freedom” loses the “ease” nuance; prefer “great freedom and ease.”
- “opened up boundless compassion and wisdom” — “opened up” is odd for 开启; prefer “awakened” or “brought forth.”

### Q03 怎么找到适合自己的法门

Quoted text: `But this variety of choices is not necessarily beneficial for beginners.`

- OK, but “this variety of choices” could be “so many choices.”

Quoted text: `Yet the feelings of ordinary beings are impermanent and changeable, so many people become keen on running from temple to temple looking for teachers, traveling north and south, visiting everywhere.`

- “become keen on” is formal/British; prefer “become eager to” or “are eager.”
- “traveling north and south, visiting everywhere” is literal; prefer “traveling far and wide.”
- Sentence is long; split.

Quoted text: `so that you will not be biased toward one extreme or miss the point`

- 偏执一端 or 不得要领: “biased toward one extreme” is redundant. Prefer “go to extremes or miss the point.”

Quoted text: `Three-Stage Practice is a popular system of study and practice designed to address these problems, similar to a general curriculum`

- “popular” for 大众化 can mean “well-liked”; here it means “for the general public.” Prefer “mass-oriented” or “public.”

### Q04 学佛该从学儒开始吗

Quoted text: `Do people today still need this? I do not think so necessarily.`

- Awkward word order; prefer “I don’t think so” or “Not necessarily.”

Quoted text: `the Buddhadharma itself also has a perfect human ethics`

- “perfect human ethics” overstates 完善; prefer “complete human ethics” or “well-developed ethical system.”

### Q05 博采众长需要高度

Quoted text: `Once we have the view of the Dharma, all dharmas can become Dharma.`

- Accurate but abstract. Could be smoother: “When we have the Dharma view, all phenomena can become Dharma.”

Quoted text: `this view represents a height of understanding about life`

- OK, but “a height of understanding” is slightly stiff; “a higher understanding of life” is more natural.

Quoted text: `they are still the crystallized wisdom of wise ones ancient and modern, Chinese and foreign, and can inspire and serve as reference for many people.`

- “serve as reference” is not idiomatic; prefer “provide guidance” or “serve as a reference.”

Quoted text: `if you do not have strong ability to assimilate them, reading too much can easily lead to indigestion`

- Metaphor is preserved; “indigestion” works.

Quoted text: `you should concentrate your energy and go deeply into one door, and only later, if you truly have extra strength, is it not too late to read widely.`

- Inverted clause “is it not too late” is awkward; prefer “it is not too late to read widely.”

Quoted text: `If at the start you stretch your front too long, you may find your strength insufficient.`

- 把战线拉得很长 / 力有不逮：idiomatic English is “spread yourself too thin” or “overextend yourself.”

Quoted text: `using content they are interested in as an entry point can arouse resonance`

- “arouse resonance” is literal; prefer “resonate” or “strike a chord.”

### Q06 信仰是自由的

Quoted text: `Faith is free: you can choose something, or choose not to.`

- “choose something” is vague; prefer “you may choose a faith, or choose none.”

Quoted text: `our understanding improves along with the broadening of our horizons`

- Wordy; prefer “our understanding grows as our horizons broaden.”

Quoted text: `If you make a new choice because you feel the wisdom of the Dharma is more ultimate, this is perfectly normal.`

- “more ultimate” is awkward; “more complete” or “more profound” is smoother (though 究竟 has a technical sense, in this spoken context “more complete” reads better).

Quoted text: `the Three Jewels of Buddha, Dharma, and Sangha can serve as a reliance for all future time`

- 尽未来际：terms DB has no exact entry, but “for all future time” is literal. Prefer “for all future lives” or “throughout all future time.”

Quoted text: `not merely taking refuge on the basis of some feeling, which leaves one always worried about personal gains and losses`

- “worried about personal gains and losses” for 患得患失 is acceptable but stiff; “always anxious about gain and loss” is closer.

### Q07 带着问题来选择

Quoted text: `I deeply know that straddling two boats is wrong`

- “I deeply know” is not idiomatic; prefer “I know full well” or “I am keenly aware.”
- “straddling two boats” is understandable but not natural; prefer “trying to walk two paths” or “riding two boats.”

Quoted text: `you will sink deeper and deeper into "choice difficulty"`

- 选择困难症：prefer “decision paralysis” or “choice paralysis.”

### Q08 信佛后能否去其他宗教场所

Quoted text: `I am Hui, and I should believe in Islam`

- “I am Hui” is acceptable, but “I am Hui Muslim” or “I am a Hui” may be clearer for readers unfamiliar with the term.

Quoted text: `the present is an age of loss of faith`

- 信仰缺失：OK, but “an age of fading faith” is more natural.

Quoted text: `It is related to the decade of catastrophe, to long-standing education, and also to weakness in the propagation of the Dharma by the religious community.`

- “decade of catastrophe” for 十年浩劫 is euphemistic and may be unclear; readers may need context. Consider a gloss or note if the target audience is international.
- “propagation of the Dharma by the religious community” — “religious community” is vague; “Buddhist community” or “Sangha” is clearer.

### Q09 想出家该怎么做

Quoted text: `For yourself, you must have a correct understanding of becoming a monastic.`

- “For yourself” is slightly odd; prefer “First, for yourself…” or “Personally…”

Quoted text: `It is not only leaving the worldly household, but even more leaving the household of the five aggregates, leaving the household of birth and death, leaving the household of samsara.`

- Parallel structure is good but repetitive; could be tightened: “not only leaving the worldly home, but even more the home of the five aggregates, of birth and death, and of samsara.”

Quoted text: `they feel you truly wish to cultivate, can adapt to, and will abide by the rules of the monastery`

- “wish to cultivate” is vague; 修行 here is broader. “are sincere in your practice” is better.

### Q10 以建寺造像开发旅游如法吗

Quoted text: `many temples are now also keen on tourism development`

- “keen on” again; prefer “eagerly pursuing” or “enthusiastically pursuing.”

Quoted text: `great wise teachers`

- 大善知识：redundant; prefer “great teachers,” “wise teachers,” or “authentic teachers.”

Quoted text: `choose wise teachers who are worthy of reliance`

- Awkward; prefer “choose wise teachers in whom we can place our trust” or “rely on wise teachers.”

Quoted text: `I believe that the external conditions we attract will also change.`

- 感得的外缘：OK, but “the conditions we draw to ourselves will also change” is smoother.

---

## Chapter 2 — 忆念三宝 / II. Recollecting the Three Jewels

### Q01–Q02 念佛与见佛 / 佛有寿命吗

Quoted text: `What is seen in the Surangama section and the Amitabha Sutra is the enjoyment body of the Buddha`

- 报身 is rendered as “enjoyment body” (Skt. *sambhogakāya*), which is standard in academic sources. MPI usage often prefers “reward body.” Verify target convention.

Quoted text: `The enjoyment body is formed from the Buddha's wisdom and merit.`

- “formed from” is slightly mechanical; “embodied wisdom and merit” or “arises from” reads more naturally.

Quoted text: `at the age of eighty entered nirvana in the sala grove`

- 入灭 for the historical Buddha is more precisely “entered parinirvana”; “entered nirvana” is acceptable but less specific.

### Q06 观修是为了强化信心

Quoted text: `with every sound entering the ears`

- 声声入耳 is an idiom meaning the recitation is clearly heard/attended to; the literal rendering is understandable but flat. Consider “with every syllable clearly heard.”

---

## Chapter 3 — 以戒为师 / III. Taking the Precepts as Teacher

### Q01 没有谁管谁的管理

Quoted text: `purely public-interest organization`

- “Public-interest organization” is accurate but clunky; “non-profit” or “charitable organization” is more natural.

Quoted text: `patterned, standardized way of study and practice`

- “Patterned” is odd in English; “structured, standardized” or “model-based, standardized” is clearer.

Quoted text: `This also accords with the traditional Buddhist way of management.`

- “Way of management” is awkward; prefer “approach to management” or “style of governance.”

Quoted text: `The Dharma is the wisdom of the Buddhadharma and the path of cultivation`

- Repetition of “Dharma / Buddhadharma” in one sentence is heavy; tighten to “the wisdom of the Dharma and the path of cultivation.”

### Q02 持戒困难怎么办

Quoted text: `Our present life is a product of ignorance, chaotic and disorderly.`

- Inversion after the noun phrase is awkward; prefer “a product of ignorance—chaotic and disorderly.”

Quoted text: `This conflict makes the ordinary mind feel repressed`

- 凡夫心 is the mind of an ordinary being; “ordinary mind” can be misleading (Chan uses “ordinary mind” differently). Prefer “the mind of an ordinary being.”

Quoted text: `Cultivation is the correction of mental states, character, and the quality of life through correcting our views and behavior.`

- “Correction … through correcting” is repetitive. Prefer “Cultivation transforms our mental states, character, and the quality of life by correcting our views and behavior.”

### Q04 受戒后可以参战吗

Quoted text: `if special circumstances are encountered, there is an allowance for this.`

- Passive and abstract; prefer “special circumstances may create an exception.”

Quoted text: `the bodhisattva's resolve is completely different from that of a knight-errant.`

- 侠客 is more commonly “knight-errant” in wuxia contexts; here “vigilante” or “chivalrous hero” may be clearer for Western readers.

### Q05 众生真的平等吗

Quoted text: `Sentient beings are equal and also not equal.`

- Accurate but terse to the point of being cryptic; consider “Sentient beings are equal in one sense, yet not equal in another.”

Quoted text: `the starting point of each life is not the same`

- 起点 refers to karmic starting conditions; “starting point” is fine but “karmic starting point” adds clarity.

### Q06 喜欢吃肉怎么治

Quoted text: `If you are attached to meat, you can begin by transforming your views through reflection.`

- OK, but “overcome your attachment to meat” would be more direct.

### Q07 做股票犯不犯盗戒

Quoted text: `stock trading can be either investment-oriented or speculation-oriented`

- Awkward compound adjectives; prefer “investing or speculating” or “investment-based or speculation-based.”

Quoted text: `because of the eagerness for quick success`

- 急功近利 is “eager for quick success and instant benefit”; the rendering misses “benefit.” Prefer “because of the eagerness for quick gains.”

### Q08 不妄语的界定

Quoted text: `do not speak merely to show off your own cleverness`

- 逞口舌之快 is closer to “speak for the thrill of it” or “indulge in sharp talk”; “show off your own cleverness” is acceptable but not quite the idiom.

### Q09 怎么面对不如法的现象

Quoted text: `drawing near to wise teachers and to rely on them`

- Parallelism error: “drawing near” should be “draw near.”

Quoted text: `Irresponsible discussion`

- 妄加议论 is “reckless discussion” or “idle criticism”; “irresponsible discussion” is acceptable but “reckless talk” is punchier.

### Q10 持戒是看清现实后的自觉选择

Quoted text: `influenced by the liberation of individuality`

- 个性解放 is “individual liberation” or “emancipation of the individual”; “liberation of individuality” is slightly off.

Quoted text: `indulgence, willfulness, and acting as one pleases have become the norm`

- 我行我素 is “doing as one pleases”; the phrase already covers willfulness, so the three terms partly overlap. Tighten.

### Q11 罪业也是缘起法

Quoted text: `To err is human.`

- 人非圣贤，孰能无过 means “To err is human” but is more formal/literary; the translation captures the sense but loses the Buddhist register. Acceptable.

Quoted text: `psychological burden is not a positive emotion`

- 心理负担 is “mental burden,” not an emotion. Prefer “mental burden is not a wholesome state.”

Quoted text: `the power of eradication, which destroys present conduct; the power of remedy, which counteracts present conduct`

- “Destroys present conduct / counteracts present conduct” is repetitive and unclear. The four powers of confession are standard; use standard terminology if available (e.g., power of remorse / support / restraint / reliance / refuge).

---

## Chapter 4 — 态度方法 / IV. Attitudes and Methods

### Q01 策励精进的善因缘

Quoted text: `Faced with this pincer attack from within and without`

- “Pincer attack” is vivid but militaristic; in this pastoral context, “pressure from within and without” or “assault from both sides” is smoother.

Quoted text: `The stalemate you are in now`

- 胶着状态 is indeed “stalemate,” but in a spiritual context “stuck place” or “impasse” may feel more natural.

Quoted text: `listening to it often and entering into contemplation as you follow the text can spur you to diligent practice`

- Wordy; “listening often and contemplating along with the text can spur diligence.”

### Q02 发愿要具体吗

Quoted text: `Because it is the ultimate goal, it is naturally general.`

- 笼统 here means “broad/abstract,” not “general” in a pejorative sense. Prefer “naturally broad.”

Quoted text: `Samantabhadra's ten great vows`

- Standard; confirm whether MPI style is “Ten Great Vows of Samantabhadra.”

### Q03 学以致用才是真进步

Quoted text: `Once you are on the path, simply follow the guidance honestly; there is no need to run here and there.`

- “Run here and there” is literal for 东跑西跑; “chase after other methods” or “run around” is smoother.

Quoted text: `If you dabble in things or cling to all sorts of external pursuits`

- 浅尝辄止 is “dabble”; 攀缘 is “cling to external objects/conditions.” The rendering is acceptable but “external pursuits” dilutes the Buddhist sense of *ālambana*. Prefer “cling to all sorts of external conditions.”

### Q04 诵经离不开基础

Quoted text: `Whether you should persevere in one sutra depends on whether that sutra suits you.`

- 一门深入 is “go deeply into one door/gate”; “persevere in one sutra” is OK but loses the metaphor. Prefer “whether you should go deeply into one sutra.”

Quoted text: `if from the start you simply cling to a sutra or a Buddha's name and recite it muddle-headedly`

- “Muddle-headedly” is a rare adverb; “in a muddled way” or “without understanding” is better.

### Q05 打坐怎么克服身体障碍

Quoted text: `The key to sitting meditation is making good use of the mind; posture is only an auxiliary means of directing the mind.`

- 善用其心 is “making good use of the mind,” but the phrase is repeated from the chapter title. OK.

Quoted text: `We gradually move from inferential cognition to direct perception.`

- 比量 / 现量 are standard Buddhist epistemological terms; the translation is clear.

Quoted text: `it is often like the tree wishing stillness while the wind keeps blowing`

- The idiom 树欲静而风不止 is usually rendered “the tree may crave stillness, but the wind will not cease.” The current version is understandable but less elegant.

### Q06 功夫需要训练

Quoted text: `When the skill has been thoroughly applied, the power of mindfulness will grow stronger day by day`

- 功夫用熟了 is “when the skill becomes proficient”; “thoroughly applied” is slightly off. Prefer “when proficiency develops.”

### Q07 内外兼修，保持修学状态

Quoted text: `material life is so abundant, and greed, hatred, and delusion constantly occupy the mind`

- Awkward sentence fragment after the semicolon; restructure: “material life is abundant, and greed, hatred, and delusion constantly dominate the mind.”

Quoted text: `atmosphere in which everyone supports and empowers one another`

- 加持 is “empowerment/blessing”; “empowers one another” is OK but loses the religious nuance. “Supports and blesses one another” may be closer.

---

## Chapter 5 — 菩提路上 / V. On the Bodhi Path

### Q01 禅修和皈依定课

Quoted text: `I am studying in the Tongxi Class`

- 同喜班 is typically left as “Tongxi Class” in MPI materials; verify if glossary requires translation.

Quoted text: `it is often like the tree wishing stillness while the wind keeps blowing`

- Same idiom issue as Chapter 4; prefer standard rendering.

### Q02 想到就要做到

Quoted text: `Being able to see your shortcomings, your inner desires, and your demonic side`

- 魔性 is “demonic nature” or “mara-like tendencies”; “demonic side” is acceptable but a bit comic-book.

Quoted text: `Some people feel urgent but do not act urgently; that is useless.`

- 想起来很急，做起来又不急了 is “urgent in thought but not in deed”; current rendering is awkward. Prefer “Some people feel a sense of urgency but don't act urgently; that is useless.”

### Q03 考量自己的根机

Quoted text: `Chan is designed for those of sharp and keen faculties`

- “Sharp and keen faculties” is redundant. Prefer “those of sharp faculties” or “those of keen faculties.”

Quoted text: `even a wise teacher cannot lift you up`

- 提点不了 is “cannot guide/point out”; “lift you up” is too physical. Prefer “cannot guide you.”

Quoted text: `Later generations of Chan students, because their obstacles were deep and wisdom shallow and they had no guide, ended up with mere "lip-service Chan," or even used it as an excuse to be lazy.`

- “Lip-service Chan” for 口头禅 is excellent. The sentence is long but clear.

### Q04 检验修行的标准

Quoted text: `Using relics to check seems a little too late.`

- 通过舍利子来检验似乎晚了点 — the rendering is fine, but “Using relics as a measure seems rather late in the day” is more idiomatic.

Quoted text: `Does this mean practice is an unknowable mysticism?`

- 玄学 here is “mystery/esoteric art,” not “mysticism.” Prefer “an unknowable mystery.”

### Q05 只有往生净土这条路吗

Quoted text: `lay practitioners can attain the third fruit`

- 三果 is the third fruit (*anāgāmi*); standard. OK.

Quoted text: `reciting the Buddha's name and seeking rebirth in the Pure Land is the safer choice`

- 保险 is “safer/more secure”; OK.

### Q06 依止和广学

Quoted text: `Merely requesting the Dharma does not yet constitute a relationship of reliance.`

- 依止关系 is “reliance relationship” — acceptable in Buddhist English but “teacher-student relationship” may be clearer.

Quoted text: `the ten qualities of a qualified teacher in the Lamrim`

- 《略论》 is *Lamrim*; OK.

Quoted text: `you yourself must also possess the marks of a disciple`

- 弟子相 is “marks of a disciple”; standard.

### Q07 如何在生活中实践佛法

Quoted text: `establish actions corresponding to liberation`

- 和解脱相应的行为 is “actions in harmony with liberation” or “actions conducive to liberation.” “Corresponding to” is vague.

Quoted text: `every place becomes a place of practice`

- 道场 is “place of practice,” but the repetition is awkward. “Everywhere becomes a field of practice.”

### Q08 什么身份适合修行

Quoted text: `Going forth carries few worldly burdens`

- 出家 = going forth; standard.

Quoted text: `influenced by economic tides`

- 经济浪潮 is “economic waves/tides”; the metaphor is preserved. OK.

Quoted text: `in the midst of the rolling red dust`

- 红尘滚滚 is “rolling red dust”; the idiom is preserved literally. Acceptable for Buddhist register.

---

## Chapter 6 — 闻思正法 / VI. Hearing and Contemplating the True Dharma

### Q01 觉醒之后去哪儿

Quoted text: `the Pure Land is not regarded as a permanent destination, but as a place for further cultivation`

- Clear and accurate.

Quoted text: `Ordinary beings drift through samsara driven by karma, unable to control their course`

- Good rendering of 身不由己.

### Q02 净土到底有没有

Quoted text: `Madhyamaka teaches dependent origination and emptiness of nature`

- 缘起性空 is “dependent origination and emptiness of self-nature”; current is OK.

Quoted text: `Consciousness-Only teaches that all dharmas are mind-only`

- Standard.

Quoted text: `Tiantai teaches three thousand realms in a single thought`

- Standard.

Quoted text: `ordinary beings take it as solid and real`

- 实实在在 is “solid and real”; OK.

### Q03 有多少个世界

Quoted text: `each wears their own colored glasses and inhabits a unique, differentiated world`

- Good.

Quoted text: `Learning Buddhism helps us remove these colored glasses`

- 有色眼镜 is “colored glasses”; OK.

### Q04 无为法也有差别吗

Quoted text: `Nothing Attained, Nothing Spoken`

- 无得无说分 — verify standard English title of this chapter; some translations use “No Attainment, No Teaching.”

Quoted text: `the perfectly realized nature`

- Standard for 圆成实性.

### Q05 能观和所观

Quoted text: `When the mind produces this duality, it becomes caught in attachment to it.`

- 能所 is “subject and object” or “observer and observed”; current is clear.

Quoted text: `When mind is empty and objects are still`

- 心空境寂 is poetic; current rendering is good.

### Q06 自性、法性、空性、佛性

Quoted text: `The self-nature spoken of from the perspective of conventional truth is what the Dharma rejects.`

- 世俗谛 is “conventional truth”; standard.

Quoted text: `The Heart Sutra repeatedly emphasizes no, without, and empty`

- 不、无、空 — the rendering is a bit list-like but clear.

Quoted text: `representing the awakened power inherently present within life`

- 本自具足的觉醒力量 — “awakened power inherently present within life” is wordy. Prefer “the awakened power inherent in life.”

### Q07 普贤行愿乃真功德

Quoted text: `Seeing the nature is gong; equality is de`

- Good handling of 功 / 德.

Quoted text: `fields of blessing`

- 福田 is “field of blessing/merit”; standard.

### Q08 见和不见

Quoted text: `emptiness and appearance are not in opposition`

- 空性和显现不是对立的 — “not in opposition” is fine; “not contradictory” is also possible.

Quoted text: `The sutra takes the arousing of mind without attachment as the essence of practice`

- 无住生心 — standard rendering.

### Q09 不识本心，学法无益

Quoted text: `Clear mind and seeing the nature`

- 明心见性 is “clear mind and seeing the nature”; standard MPI rendering? Usually “clearing the mind and seeing the nature.”

Quoted text: `the Twelve Links of Dependent Origination`

- Standard.

Quoted text: `only surface appearance`

- 表面文章 is “mere show / window dressing / surface work”; “surface appearance” misses the “insincere show” nuance. Prefer “mere outward show.”

---

## Chapter 7 — 缘起无我 / VII. Dependent Origination and No-Self

### Q01 五蕴非我，我在哪

Quoted text: `Buddhism speaks of no-self (anatman), yet it also speaks of the conventional self.`

- Good.

Quoted text: `the three natures (trisvabhava): the falsely conceived nature (parikalpita), the dependent nature (paratantra), and the perfectly realized nature (parinishpanna)`

- Technical terms are accurate.

Quoted text: `the illusion of attachment to self and dharmas gives rise to`

- 我法二执 is “attachment to self and dharmas”; OK.

### Q02 真正的我是什么

Quoted text: `When Buddhism speaks of no-self, it does not mean that you do not exist; it denies the mistaken identification with the self and guides us to truly find ourselves.`

- Slightly repetitive “self … ourselves”; restructure: “it denies our mistaken identification with a self and guides us to find what we truly are.”

Quoted text: `discover the ability to save ourselves`

- 自我拯救的能力 is “ability to save ourselves”; OK, though “capacity for self-liberation” may be more Buddhist.

### Q03 我、末那、阿赖耶和佛性

Quoted text: `Manas and Alaya come from the Consciousness-Only teaching of the eight consciousnesses`

- Standard.

Quoted text: `Cognition and Existence`

- 《认识与存在》 — verify title; if this is a published translation, use that title.

Quoted text: `Thirty Verses on Consciousness-Only`

- Standard for 《唯识三十论》.

### Q04 克隆只是出生方式不同

Quoted text: `Human cloning is banned worldwide, for it raises numerous moral, ethical, and other problems`

- Good.

Quoted text: `there is also a consciousness that goes to be reborn`

- 识去投胎 — “a consciousness that goes to be reborn” is literal but clear.

### Q05 轮回和解脱

Quoted text: `Rebirth is a shared premise of Indian culture.`

- 共识 is “shared premise/consensus”; “shared premise” is good.

Quoted text: `believe only what they see`

- 看到才肯相信 — “believe only what they see”; OK.

Quoted text: `our cognitive system has great limitations and distortions`

- 局限性和错乱性 — “limitations and distortions” is good.

Quoted text: `The doctrine of rebirth can answer these questions. Without rebirth, many phenomena would be inexplicable.`

- Clear.

Quoted text: `But liberation from rebirth does not mean that everything is annihilated or that one enters a state of nihilistic emptiness.`

- 顽空 is “nihilistic emptiness / annihilationism”; standard.

### Q06 缘起的生命观

Quoted text: `similarly continuous, neither severed nor permanent`

- 相似相续，不断不常 — the rendering is accurate but technical; “continuous yet ever-changing, neither annihilated nor permanent” may read better.

Quoted text: `a super hard drive that stores information`

- 超级硬盘 is “super hard drive”; the modern metaphor is preserved. OK.

Quoted text: `the dependent-origination view of life, which differs both from the eternalism of ordinary religions and from the annihilationism of materialism`

- Excellent.

### Q07 业果怎么延续到来世

Quoted text: `there are present reward, next-life reward, and later reward`

- 现报、生报、后报 — “present reward, next-life reward, and later reward” is acceptable; more standard is “reward in this life, next life, or a future life.”

Quoted text: `the continuative result of such mental conduct`

- 等流果 is “continuative result / result of equal outflow”; technical, OK.

### Q08 果报还自受

Quoted text: `once these karmic rewards are exhausted, they end and do not continue endlessly`

- Wordy; “once exhausted, they end and do not continue.”

Quoted text: `Falling into hell only repays the largest debt, not all of them`

- Mixed singular/plural; “largest debt” vs “all of them.” Prefer “only repays the largest debt, not every debt.”

---

## Chapter 8 — 人生正见 / VIII. Right View of Life

### Q01 什么是真正的成功

Quoted text: `a more ultimate success`

- Same issue as Chapter 1; prefer “a higher success” or “a more complete success.”

Quoted text: `the height of fame, the number of followers`

- Good parallel structure.

### Q02 怎么找到人生使命

Quoted text: `I have also asked myself what I truly want, but my heart feels empty.`

- Good.

Quoted text: `Some philosophers and artists even took the road to ruin after achieving fame and success.`

- 绝路 is “road to ruin / dead end”; OK.

Quoted text: `no longer had any interest in merely surviving in this world`

- 苟活 is “merely surviving / living on”; OK.

### Q03 何为人成即佛成

Quoted text: `When a Human Is Perfected, Buddhahood Is Perfected`

- 人成即佛成 — standard rendering.

Quoted text: `ritualization, spiritism, and otherworldliness`

- 经忏化、鬼神化、来世化 — “spiritism” for 鬼神化 is good; verify target convention.

### Q04 怎么都好，不需要烦恼

Quoted text: `The monastic environment is relatively simple, free from the constraints of various relationships and from the complexity of society`

- Good.

Quoted text: `doing great things`

- 做大事 — OK.

### Q05 三观决定人生

Quoted text: `view of life, view of the world, and values`

- 人生观、世界观、价值观 — standard.

Quoted text: `Establishing the three outlooks is not the same as learning knowledge; it can begin at any stage.`

- Clear.

---

## Chapter 9 — 人际关系 / IX. Interpersonal Relationships

### Q01 尊重缘起，勇敢做自己

Quoted text: `responding to conditions`

- 随缘 — standard, but sometimes “in harmony with conditions” flows better.

Quoted text: `forceful and opinionated`

- 强势而偏执 — “opinionated” is mild for 偏执; prefer “forceful and dogmatic” or “domineering and inflexible.”

Quoted text: `oppressive feelings, anger, and other negative emotions`

- Good.

### Q02 沟通而不是对立

Quoted text: `Being born into a less-than-ideal family environment does bring much helplessness`

- “bring much helplessness” is awkward; “can leave one feeling helpless” is better.

Quoted text: `accept reality rather than set yourself in opposition`

- “set yourself in opposition” is wordy; “rather than oppose it.”

### Q03 与父母相处的双全法

Quoted text: `your idea is not a spur-of-the-moment impulse`

- 一时兴起 — “spur-of-the-moment impulse” is redundant; “spur-of-the-moment idea.”

Quoted text: `put their minds at ease`

- 放心 — good idiom.

Quoted text: `quiet, pervasive influence, like rain soaking into the earth unnoticed`

- 润物细无声 — excellent.

### Q04 想好自己要什么

Quoted text: `older unmarried young people`

- 大龄青年 — awkward; “older singles” or “unmarried adults” is more natural.

Quoted text: `Buddhism does not say you must marry, nor does it oppose marriage`

- Clear.

Quoted text: `make the family your training ground`

- 道场 as “training ground”; OK.

Quoted text: `transcendental liberation`

- 出世解脱 — “transcendental liberation” is acceptable; “liberation from the world” is more literal.

### Q05 和孩子共同成长的功课

Quoted text: `Many parents wear themselves out with worry over their children`

- 操碎了心 — good idiom.

Quoted text: `Even with Buddhas and bodhisattvas present in the world, they can only liberate those with whom they have karmic connections`

- Good.

### Q06 身教重于言教

Quoted text: `Society as a whole today lacks education in how to be a good person`

- Good.

Quoted text: `Such teaching by example is the most direct and often surpasses verbal instruction`

- 身教重于言教 — clear.

### Q07 从想着自己到想着他人

Quoted text: `compassion refines your mental state, improves your relationships, makes you more blessed, and more welcome`

- 更受欢迎 is “more welcome” but “more well-liked” or “more welcomed by others” is clearer.

Quoted text: `the practice of exchanging self and others`

- 自他相换 — standard.

### Q08 怎么让自己更包容

Quoted text: `the three great disasters that destroy the world—fire burning up to the heaven of the first dhyāna`

- Technical and accurate.

Quoted text: `unconditional great compassion and the great sympathy of seeing others as oneself`

- 无缘大慈、同体大悲 — standard rendering.

---

## Chapter 10 — 心行成长 / X. Growth of Mind and Conduct

### Q01 烦恼来了怎么办

Quoted text: `The word affliction means disturbance: "fan" is to agitate, and "nao" is to disorder.`

- Etymological explanation is helpful but “disorder” as a verb is odd. Prefer “'fan' means to agitate, 'nao' means to disturb.”

Quoted text: `unreasonable attention, which is erroneous thinking; and reasonable attention, which is wise thinking`

- 非理作意 / 如理作意 — “unreasonable / reasonable attention” is technically correct; “unwholesome / wholesome attention” is also common. Verify MPI convention.

### Q02 接纳逆境才能止损

Quoted text: `this way of speaking can sound heartless`

- 无情 is “heartless / lacking compassion”; OK.

Quoted text: `after being struck by one poisoned arrow, we are struck by a second`

- 毒箭喻 — standard.

Quoted text: `acceptance is the effective way to stop the loss in time`

- 止损 — “stop the loss” is financial jargon; here “limit the damage” is more natural.

### Q03 处理情绪的两项基本原则

Quoted text: `an inactivated virus`

- 灭活的病毒 — OK metaphor.

Quoted text: `pure intuition`

- 纯净的直觉 — OK.

### Q04 不自大，不自卑

Quoted text: `the arrogant will become stuck in their ways, and the inferior will sell themselves short`

- 故步自封 / 妄自菲薄 — good idioms.

Quoted text: `neither is conducive to the optimization of life`

- “Optimization of life” is technical-sounding; “flourishing of life” or “growth in life” is warmer.

Quoted text: `Caring about others' opinions`

- OK.

### Q05 让时间的使用更有价值

Quoted text: `random thoughts fly about`

- 妄想纷飞 — same as Chapter 1; prefer “wandering thoughts arise.”

Quoted text: `When time is used more valuably, your life will become more valuable.`

- “More valuably” is awkward; “When time is used more wisely, your life becomes more valuable.”

### Q06 鬼也是众生，别怕

Quoted text: `holy names have great power and blessings`

- 圣号 — “holy names” is standard.

Quoted text: `Whatever beings we encounter, our minds will hold only compassion`

- Good.

### Q07 让智慧照入梦境

Quoted text: `inverted dreams`

- 颠倒梦想 — standard.

Quoted text: `inverted delusion`

- 颠倒妄想 — “inverted delusion” is acceptable; “deluded inversion” is more literal.

Quoted text: `true suchness of all phenomena`

- 诸法如实相 — standard.

---

## Chapter 11 — 自利利他 / XI. Benefiting Self and Others

### Q01 不忘出离心，常修菩提心

Quoted text: `Transcending the world and engaging in it correspond to renunciation and bodhicitta`

- Good.

Quoted text: `only by eliminating afflictions and entering the world with a transcendent mind can we better help sentient beings`

- Clear.

Quoted text: `Otherwise, you are likely to be a clay bodhisattva`

- 泥菩萨 is “clay bodhisattva”; the idiom 泥菩萨过江 is alluded to. OK.

### Q02 利他心的度

Quoted text: `Orientation means the standard you set for yourself—whether you aspire to train as a bodhisattva. Capacity means the maximum you can do at present`

- 定位 / 能力 — the explanation is helpful.

Quoted text: `a bodhisattva who has attained the grounds and realized emptiness`

- 登地菩萨 — “attained the grounds” is standard.

Quoted text: `when there is a large gap between aspiration, capacity, and realization, forcing ourselves to act is harmful to both others and ourselves`

- Good.

### Q03 愿心要真要切

Quoted text: `When this aspiration is strong, your ability will quickly grow.`

- Good.

Quoted text: `truly felt and strongly desired`

- 真切 — clear.

### Q04 因为理解，所以慈悲

Quoted text: `social values today are declining`

- 社会风气不好 — “social values are declining” is a bit strong; “social morals are declining” or “social ethos is poor.”

Quoted text: `those with twisted characters, even those with corrupt morality`

- Good.

### Q05 磨刀不误砍柴工

Quoted text: `Whether one is busy is relative. Whatever you consider more important, you will find time for.`

- Clear.

Quoted text: `volunteer teams cannot keep going mainly because their thinking is not unified and the results are barely satisfactory`

- 差强人意 is “barely satisfactory / just passable”; OK.

Quoted text: `study and practice are like sharpening the ax before cutting wood`

- 磨刀不误砍柴工 — standard idiom.

---

## Chapter 12 — 工作即修行 / XII. Work Itself Is Practice

### Q01 用缘起智慧和利他心做管理

Quoted text: `Many companies today reflect their boss's culture`

- 老板文化 — “boss's culture” is literal; OK.

Quoted text: `Japan's Kazuo Inamori guided corporate management with the Dharma`

- 稻盛和夫 — verify romanization; “Kazuo Inamori” is standard.

Quoted text: `treat the company as an extension of self-grasping`

- 我执的延伸 — clear.

### Q02 正确发心，善用其心

Quoted text: `pursuits are nothing but confusion and affliction as their basis`

- Awkward; “pursuits are grounded in confusion and affliction.”

Quoted text: `In this cycle of delusion, karma, and suffering`

- 惑业苦 — standard.

Quoted text: `we cultivate merit through altruism and refine the mind through right mindfulness`

- Good.

Quoted text: `from dressing and eating to carrying firewood and drawing water—all are expressions of the Way`

- 搬柴运水都是道用 — good.

### Q03 把修行带入工作和生活

Quoted text: `Doing things with bodhicitta and doing things out of self-need may look the same, but the results are completely different.`

- Clear.

Quoted text: `every matter becomes a condition that strengthens afflictions`

- 增上缘 — “condition that strengthens” is acceptable; “condition that reinforces” is better.

### Q04 慈悲生祸害

Quoted text: `Compassion breeds misfortune`

- 慈悲生祸害 — the chapter title uses the saying; OK.

Quoted text: `"indiscriminate compassion" that actually indulges unwholesome habits`

- 滥慈悲 — good.

### Q05 职业不如法怎么办

Quoted text: `choose a right-livelihood occupation`

- 正命的职业 — “right-livelihood occupation” is redundant; “right livelihood” or “occupation consistent with right livelihood.”

Quoted text: `the loss outweighs the gain`

- 得不偿失 — good idiom.

---

## Chapter 13 — 生死和无常 / XIII. Death and Impermanence

### Q01 长寿和安乐死

Quoted text: `Does research aimed at extending life have any meaning?`

- Good.

Quoted text: `wishing to spare him such heavy suffering, is willing to bear the karmic retribution of killing in order to grant his wish`

- Long but clear; tighten: “wishing to spare him such suffering, is willing to bear the karmic result of killing him.”

### Q02 怎么才能对去向有把握

Quoted text: `contemplating death itself is a supportive condition for progress in practice`

- Good.

Quoted text: `we may not last until evening`

- 朝不保夕 — “we may not last until evening” is literal; “life is precarious” is more idiomatic.

### Q03 化悲痛为力量

Quoted text: `a child died young. His mother was heartbroken and carried the body everywhere`

- Good retelling of the mustard-seed parable.

Quoted text: `keeping an ordinary mind when things go well and still keeping an ordinary mind when things go badly`

- Wordy; “keeping an ordinary mind in both good times and bad.”

### Q04 无常让我们更珍惜

Quoted text: `even the earth will one day be destroyed`

- Good.

Quoted text: `the ripening of good karma accumulated over many lives and eons`

- 多生累劫善业招感 — good.

Quoted text: `Can we still be sure of obtaining the human body and hearing the true Dharma?`

- Clear.

### Q05 算命不如做好当下

Quoted text: `work hard on the causes and let the results unfold as they may`

- 因上努力，果上随缘 — excellent.

Quoted text: `when your luck has already turned in this very moment`

- Good.

