## Chapter 16 — 总结开示 / XVI. Concluding Dharma Words

Quoted text: `Moving from a state of ordinary, lax, and indulgent mind into a regulated life of practice can be quite demanding.`

- 懈怠放逸的凡夫心状态 — “ordinary, lax, and indulgent mind” is acceptable; “ordinary mind of laxity and indulgence” is tighter.

Quoted text: `Modern people are skilled at solving problems, but even more skilled at creating them.`

- Good.

Quoted text: `inner restlessness combined with outer distractions`

- Good.

Quoted text: `These beautiful days may easily become nothing more than fond memories.`

- Good.

