## Recurring Patterns Worth Global Search-and-Replace

1. **"keen on"** → "eager to" / "enthusiastically pursuing" (appears in Ch.1, Ch.3, etc.)
2. **"great wise teachers"** → "great teachers" / "wise teachers" / "authentic teachers" (redundant; appears in Ch.1, Ch.3, etc.)
3. **"wisdom culture"** → "culture of wisdom" / "wisdom tradition" (collocation)
4. **"more ultimate"** → "more complete" / "higher" / "more profound" (Ch.1, Ch.8)
5. **"delusive thoughts still fly about"** → "delusions run wild" / "wandering thoughts arise" (Ch.1, Ch.10)
6. **"outdo animals by far"** → "animals cannot compare" / "are left far behind" (Ch.1)
7. **"arouse resonance"** → "resonate" / "strike a chord" (Ch.1)
8. **"serve as reference"** → "provide guidance" / "serve as a reference" (Ch.1)
9. **"straddling two boats"** → "riding two boats" / "trying to walk two paths" (Ch.1)
10. **"choice difficulty"** → "decision paralysis" / "choice paralysis" (Ch.1)
11. **"religious community"** → "Buddhist community" / "Sangha" (Ch.1, Ch.3)
12. **"tree wishing stillness while the wind keeps blowing"** → "the tree may crave stillness, but the wind will not cease" (Ch.4, Ch.5)
13. **"optimization of life"** → "flourishing of life" / "growth in life" (Ch.10)
14. **"right-livelihood occupation"** → "right livelihood" (Ch.12)
15. **"more valuably"** → "more wisely" (Ch.10)

---

## Summary

The translation is faithful to the Chinese and generally reads well. The main categories of improvement are:

- **Idiomatic English**: several calques and literal compounds (e.g., "keen on," "serve as reference," "choice difficulty") can be smoothed.
- **Buddhist terminology**: verify MPI-preferred renderings for 报身, 化身, 善知识, 等流果, 末法, 暇满, 定课, 八步骤三种禅修, and the standard English titles of quoted sutras/chapters.
- **Sentence rhythm**: long, multi-clause sentences that follow Chinese structure can often be split or tightened.
- **Register consistency**: spoken Q&A tone should be preserved; avoid overly formal or technical phrasing where the original is conversational.

Recommended next step: apply the recurring-pattern fixes globally, then do a focused pass on the highest-impact Chapter 1 and Chapter 10 entries.
